money to be able to afford it.

302
00:08:06,010 --> 00:08:08,060
And if the rules don't adapt?

303
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:10,010
In the same essay, he wrote:

304
00:08:10,310 --> 00:08:12,110
most people will end up worse

305
00:08:12,150 --> 00:08:13,600
off than they are today.

306
00:08:14,010 --> 00:08:15,140
Even for him,

307
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:16,830
cheap was never enough.

308
00:08:18,010 --> 00:08:19,470
So how does everyone

309
00:08:19,510 --> 00:08:20,630
get enough money?

310
00:08:20,950 --> 00:08:22,600
Three answers are on the table.

311
00:08:22,750 --> 00:08:24,560
Each has a real weakness.

312
00:08:24,830 --> 00:08:26,370
The first is the market:

313
00:08:26,510 --> 00:08:27,630
let prices fall,

314
00:08:27,670 --> 00:08:29,490
and every dollar buys more.

315
00:08:29,650 --> 00:08:30,920
It worked for your phone.

316
00:08:31,230 --> 00:08:33,220
Its weakness is the seventh tag:

317
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:34,610
wages can fall right

318
00:08:34,650 --> 00:08:35,910
along with prices.

319
00:08:36,170 --> 00:08:37,760
The second is a fund:

320
00:08:37,910 --> 00:08:39,370
everyone owns a share.

321
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:40,770
That was Altman's plan,

322
00:08:40,810 --> 00:08:43,030
paid for by exactly two things:

323
00:08:43,210 --> 00:08:45,120
big companies, and land.

324
00:08:45,710 --> 00:08:47,680
Alaska already pays its people

325
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:48,600
a yearly check

326
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:49,790
from its oil wealth:

327
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:51,980
$1,200 this year.

328
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:53,690
His plan imagined more

329
00:08:53,730 --> 00:08:55,430
than 10 times that.

330
00:08:55,770 --> 00:08:57,870
Its weakness: a fund pays

331
00:08:57,910 --> 00:08:59,540
what politics allows.

332
00:08:59,650 --> 00:09:01,130
Alaska's lawmakers now

333
00:09:01,170 --> 00:09:02,910
set the amount every year.

334
00:09:03,250 --> 00:09:04,850
The third is a check:

335
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:06,050
the government sends

336
00:09:06,090 --> 00:09:07,180
everyone money.

337
00:09:07,320 --> 00:09:09,070
Altman backed a test of it:

338
00:09:09,270 --> 00:09:11,880
$1,000 a month, for 3 years.

339
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,300
People bought basics,

340
00:09:13,340 --> 00:09:14,990
and worked a little less.

341
00:09:15,230 --> 00:09:16,960
Its weakness is the bill.

342
00:09:17,140 --> 00:09:18,660
Even Altman has changed his

343
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:20,510
own answer more than once.

344
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:23,440
So that's the order.

345
00:09:23,650 --> 00:09:25,310
Thinking falls first.

346
00:09:25,630 --> 00:09:27,540
Things follow, slowly.

347
00:09:27,920 --> 00:09:29,880
Energy holds, for now.

348
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:31,880
The ground stays hard.

349
00:09:32,170 --> 00:09:33,180
He's half right.

350
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:35,700
And that half is worth a lot.

351
00:09:36,050 --> 00:09:37,010
What's still open

352
00:09:37,050 --> 00:09:38,510
is the seventh tag.

353
00:09:38,860 --> 00:09:40,810
Prices follow the machines.

354
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:42,780
Incomes follow the rules.

355
00:09:42,890 --> 00:09:43,980
And the rules are written

356
00:09:44,020 --> 00:09:45,900
by people you elect.

357
00:09:46,110 --> 00:09:47,950
Your wage is a price too.

358
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:49,260
And cheap only makes

359
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:50,200
you richer if your

360
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:51,750
wage isn't the first

361
00:09:51,790 --> 00:09:52,790
price to fall.

362
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:54,930
This channel exists

363
00:09:54,970 --> 00:09:56,310
for one reason:

364
00:09:56,470 --> 00:09:57,320
so that the arrival

365
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:58,510
of superintelligence

366
00:09:58,550 --> 00:10:00,320
goes well for everybody.

367
00:10:00,490 --> 00:10:02,100
Cheap prices, and the income

368
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:03,060
to pay them.

369
00:10:03,100 --> 00:10:04,100
Want that too?

370
00:10:04,180 --> 00:10:05,180
Then subscribe.

